# Stable device names for the kobold MCU boards.
#
# Install:  sudo ./scripts/setup-udev.sh
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS: /dev/ttyUSB0 and /dev/ttyUSB1 swap between reboots depending
# on enumeration order. The failure mode is sending motor commands to the
# ultrasonic board, which is exactly as bad as it sounds.
#
# The drive board is deliberately the USB-C variant, because its USB-serial
# bridge chip has a different VID/PID from the other two — which makes it
# unambiguously identifiable. CH340 clones frequently share both a VID/PID AND a
# serial number, so if both your remaining boards use CH340, match them on
# physical USB port path instead (see the KERNELS example below) and always plug
# each board into the same port. Label the ports with tape.
#
# Find your values:
#   udevadm info -a -n /dev/ttyUSB0 | grep -E 'idVendor|idProduct|serial|KERNELS' | head
#
# Common bridge chips:
#   1a86:7523  CH340        (most DevKit V1 clones)
#   1a86:55d4  CH9102 / CH343 (many USB-C boards)
#   10c4:ea60  CP2102       (Silicon Labs; usually has a real serial number)

# ---- drive board: motors, encoders, IMU, cliff reflex ----
# Preferred: match by unique serial number.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1a86", ATTRS{idProduct}=="55d4", SYMLINK+="robot-drive", MODE="0666", GROUP="dialout"

# ---- sense board: ultrasonic, IR, buzzer, OLED, safety line ----
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1a86", ATTRS{idProduct}=="7523", SYMLINK+="robot-sense", MODE="0666", GROUP="dialout"

# ---- lidar (Phase 5, if fitted) ----
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="10c4", ATTRS{idProduct}=="ea60", SYMLINK+="robot-lidar", MODE="0666", GROUP="dialout"

# ---- fallback: identical boards with no distinguishing serial ----
# Uncomment, replace the port paths with yours, and comment out the rules above.
# Find the path with:  udevadm info -q path -n /dev/ttyUSB0
#SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1a86", ATTRS{idProduct}=="7523", KERNELS=="1-1.2", SYMLINK+="robot-drive", MODE="0666"
#SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1a86", ATTRS{idProduct}=="7523", KERNELS=="1-1.3", SYMLINK+="robot-sense", MODE="0666"
